:: Meal Sister Internship [activity meal] {"position":"1725,2225"}
/*
{
        id: "sister_internship",
        passage: "Meal Sister Internship",
        isActive: false,
        mealType: ["breakfast", "lunch", "dinner"],
        isImportant: true,
        dayType: ["weekday", "weekend"],
        cooldown: 0,
        once: true,
        lastSeen: -1,
        present: ["mom", "sister"],
        requirements: [
        ],
        set: [
            () => setup.getMealById("sister_internship").isActive = false,
        ]
}
   Activated by: "Internship Season" (sister_internshipSeason). She asked to do her college
   internship at my company, and I said yes.
*/
Halfway through the meal, $sister.callName pulls a folded sheet of paper out of her back pocket, smooths it flat on the table with the side of her hand and pushes it across to me, along with a pen she's clearly been carrying around all day waiting for this moment.

/* IMAGE: images/meals/important/sister_internship.jpg | An internship agreement form on the kitchen table next to a plate, a pen on top. Sister leaning across the table, chin in her hands, waiting. Mom reading the form upside down. */

It's a form from her college. INTERNSHIP AGREEMENT, it says at the top, and near the bottom there's a line that says Supervisor Signature.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Sign here, please, and here, and initial that one. Thank you, boss." },
{ who: $mom, text: "What's this?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "My internship! I'm doing it at his company. The advisor said it counts as long as I get real business experience and somebody signs off on my hours." },
{ who: $mom, text: "At the company? With your $sister.playerRelation?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Who else is going to hire someone whose biggest professional achievement is a salt shaker presentation?" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<if setup.questDone("mom_falseSympathy")>>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "So it'll be all three of us there, every day. That's... well, I'll just have to make more sandwiches, won't I." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Family business! We should get matching polo shirts." },
{ who: $mom, text: "We are not getting matching polo shirts." },
{ who: $sister, text: "You'd look so good in teal, $mom.callName." },
{ text: "$mom.callName laughs, but she also looks at me, and there's a question in it that she doesn't ask. Her $mom.playerRelation signs her paychecks. Now he's going to sign $sister.callName's hours too." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<<else>>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, that's actually a lovely idea, you two working together. I always hoped you'd find something you could do side by side." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Right? I'll make him look professional and he'll make me look smart." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Just don't let him work you to death, sweetie. He gets that from me." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<</if>>

I read the form properly, all of it, while she bounces her knee under the table. Twenty hours a week. Duties as assigned by the supervisor. Evaluation at the end of the semester, which I'll write.

I read the line about duties as assigned by the supervisor a second time.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "You know you'll have to make the coffee. That's what interns do." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I make excellent coffee. People are going to write poems about my coffee." },
{ who: $player, text: "And you'll have to listen to your boss." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I always listen to you." },
{ text: "She says it lightly, as a joke. Then she seems to hear it, and she doesn't take it back." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I sign. She snatches the form away before the ink is dry, folds it into her pocket and pats it twice, like it's money.

<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterRelation" 3>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterCorruption" 1>>
